on":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.3.stable (77dcf97d8)\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10.0.19045 - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-4930K CPU @ 3.40GHz (12 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRunning a script with the base set to zero or one e.g. \"String.num_uint64(15, 0, false)\" will either instantly crash or freeze the Godot editor. I don't see how it's useful to set the base to either zero or one, but I expected it to return an error instead of crashing/freezing Godot.\r\n\r\nInitially I wanted to find a way to convert binary numbers, and after finding this method I tested it and found it was crashing the editor. \r\nNote: Base set to a negative integer initially returned an error, but opening Godot after a crash and looping through (e.g. 0-1000) gives me 0-9, A-Z, some common symbols, a-z, more symbols etc. I don't know if this is important or not.\r\n\r\n\r\nGodot Docs:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_string.html#class-string-method-num-uint64\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\r\n@tool\r\nextends EditorScript\r\n\r\nfunc _run() -> void:\r\n\ttest()\r\n\r\n#This will instantly crash Godot\r\nfunc test() -> void:\r\n\tvar a:String\r\n\ta = String.num_uint64(15, 0) #When base = 0\r\n\r\n#This will freeze Godot\r\nfunc test() -> void:\r\n\tvar a:String\r\n\ta = String.num_uint64(15, 0) #When base = 1\r\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://